Follow-up commit: 05e0067451798f54f148c954a722bfd16a4e430d (parent 21115d0480dbf68dc4a86e5e4f5c1ebbe108b9a4)
Code inspection confirms all four findings: stale installed snapshot deletes and omits newly listed distros; old probes can be accepted after rescan or observed stop/start; concurrent calls duplicate probes and failure completion resets retry timing; no concurrency regression test existed. These interleavings were inspected, not executed.
The fix uses the current listing for output and cleanup, identifies in-flight probes and invalidates them on rescan, observed stop or removal. Concurrent ordinary readers do not launch duplicate probes; a rescan can start a fresh probe while an invalidated one is still running. The stop/start protection requires the stopped state to have been observed by a running-list refresh.
Added internal/agent/wsl_probe_lock_windows_test.go with channel-controlled scenarios for list change and persistence, rescan, observed stop/start, and duplicate readers. Tests have not been run; there is no red/green or Windows runtime evidence. No Windows environment was faked.
